From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shill: ignore Waydroid's bridge, as ARC's

NickelOS runs Android in Waydroid, which puts Android on a bridge of its
own, waydroid0, with its own DHCP and DNS (dnsmasq) and NAT. shill took
the bridge for a new network device; dns-proxy then failed on it ("Device
/device/waydroid0 ... NetworkConfig is not ...") and the device's DNS
stayed broken until a reboot. ARC's bridges (arc_*) and veth pairs are
already left to their owners by name; add Waydroid's.

---
--- a/shill/device_info.cc
+++ b/shill/device_info.cc
@@ -152,6 +152,10 @@
     // for now.
     "arc_",
     "veth",
+    // NickelOS: Waydroid's bridge (waydroid0) is Android's private network,
+    // as ARC's are. Managed as a network of its own, it took the DNS proxy
+    // down with it.
+    "waydroid",
 };
 
 // As of Linux v5.4, these "kinds" are not part of a UAPI header definition, so
